# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Asmita Jana et al. (2026). Benchmarking machine-learned potentials for adsorption on Pt and $$\textrm{IrO}_2$$ surfaces using OC20 and OMat24.
#   Discover Chemistry.. doi:10.1007/s44371-026-00865-5
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 bc89392b27d45122...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 370 (Dataset/benchmark). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/jana2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the pretrained uma-s-1p1 checkpoint (FAIRChem, ASE
# LBFGS to 0.001 eV/A) with the OC20 task for CO, NO, O and H on
# Pt(111), Pt(110) and Pt(231), and with the OMat24 task for H, O and OH
# on O-terminated IrO2(110), compared with VASP RPBE (Pt, spin-polarised
# and non-spin-polarised) and PBE+D3 (IrO2) adsorption energies. The text
# gives only approximate agreement ('within about 0.1, 0.2, 0.3 eV');
# the per-adsorbate values are in SI tables, so no metrics are encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

entity:study-jana2026 a mlips:BenchmarkStudy ;
    rdfs:label "Jana et al. (2026): benchmarking UMA (OC20 and OMat24 tasks) for adsorption energies on Pt and IrO2 surfaces against DFT" ;
    mlips:reportedIn entity:article-jana2026 .

entity:article-jana2026 a schema:ScholarlyArticle ;
